# Build context exclusions: buffer databases and build cruft. The context is shared by the bridge
# and API images, so exclusions target only files that should never be distributed — database files,
# bytecode, and build artifacts — not code that particular images use.
#
# Beyond image size, this is a safety boundary: buffer databases hold real observations in transit and
# must never end up in an image that gets pushed to a registry.
#
# A pattern is matched from the root of the context: `*.db` would exclude only a database next to the
# Dockerfile, and `scripts/run_bridge.py` / `scripts/run_nce_bridge.py` default `--db` to a relative
# path — a buffer started from `scripts/` or `src/` would be copied into both images. Hence `**/`
# (any depth, the root included). tests/test_docker_build_context.py keeps these lines here.
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
tests/
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
